## Inference lifetime and result semantics

`InferenceQueue` exposes await-only conveniences and explicit submission APIs.
Use `submit_*` when the caller owns one job; use `*_with_cancellation` when
several jobs belong to one search, import, embedding, chat, or sandbox
operation.

- Create one `queue::CancellationToken` at the parent boundary and clone it
  into every child job.
- Keep the GPUI/async owner alive until completion is observed. Dropping a
  result receiver is a safety fallback, not the primary contract.
- Check cancellation before graph or vector writes. Provider completion after
  cancellation must not commit stale work.
- Preserve `InferenceError::{Cancelled, Superseded, TimedOut,
  ProviderFailed, WorkerDropped, CapabilityUnavailable}` instead of flattening
  them into an `anyhow` string too early.
- Cancellation does not train embedding EWMA and does not count as successful
  service. Queue counters are content-free and saturating.

Workers check the token while pending, during embedding retry backoff, model
activation, provider futures, first-token/stream reads, and bounded batch
fan-out. Retry delays and EWMA fallback are evidence-retained constants; change
them only with the deterministic scenarios in
`crates/u-forge-core/benches/inference_lifecycle.rs` and queue tests.

