## Agent tool validation and budgets

Tool args in `u-forge-agent` are validated against JSON Schema before deserialization. Do not call `serde_json::from_value` directly on a raw tool arg payload — call `tool_validation::validate_tool_args(tool_name, &raw)?` first. The validated value is then safe to deserialize into the typed Args struct.

The graph agent applies one model-reconciled `EffectiveAgentBudget` per request.
It accounts for system/tool definitions, whole-record schema selection,
retained history, response reserve, each model turn, tool arguments, and
model-visible tool output through the shared cached token estimator. Limits
are fitted independently for every provider call; do not reintroduce a
cumulative token ceiling across a valid multi-turn request.

- Never concatenate `schema_prompt_summary_all()` into a request. Use
  `bounded_schema_summary`; schema records and JSON are never byte-sliced.
- Fit the newest structurally valid history suffix before every model dispatch.
- Bound tool output at semantic record boundaries and include omission counts
  or continuation guidance. This bound is per result and model-window-aware.
- Fingerprint the validated tool name + canonical JSON arguments. Identical
  unchanged reads consume the repeat allowance; corrected arguments, changed
  results, and committed graph mutations count as progress.
- Budget and repeat stops are deliberate `ChatEvent` outcomes, not transport
  failures. Diagnostics expose aggregate counts only, never prompt content.
